# Create an exercise. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" and "List the groups" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### List the groups → 200. The requests below use the first two.
# @name groups
GET {{host}}/api/v1/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A new exercise → 201 with a Location. Send it twice: the second time is 409 exercise.name_taken.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bench press",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "alsoWorksGroupIds": ["{{groups.response.body.$[1].id}}"]
}

### The same name in another case → 409 exercise.name_taken.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "BENCH PRESS",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"
}

### Also works includes its own group → 400 validation, with an error for alsoWorksGroupIds.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pec deck",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "alsoWorksGroupIds": ["{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"]
}

### A group that does not exist → 404 group.not_found.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pec deck",
  "groupId": "0198a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000"
}

### No name → 400 validation, with an error for name.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": " ",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"
}

### Not signed in → 401 unauthorized.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pec deck",
  "groupId": "0198a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000"
}
